# L §5.12 example fill, copied (payers an index, the years a year index 2020..2023, carry_years = 1).  Arcs for ewa:
# supply year o to demand year t with t >= o - 1 and t - o <= 1.  Sorted by (o, t): (2020, 2020), (2020, 2021),
# (2021, 2020), (2021, 2021), (2021, 2022), ...  Supplies 100, 50; rooms 30, 80, 80, 0.  Takes: min(100, 30) = 30
# (R = 70, Q2020 = 0); min(70, 80) = 70 (R = 0, Q2021 = 10); (2021, 2020): Q = 0, 0; min(50, 10) = 10 (R = 40);
# min(40, 80) = 40.  Pairs that aren't arcs take 0 (Outputs).
# With credit[ewa, 2020] a stated hole: its takes are holes ("a hole side ... makes the take a hole"); after them R
# and Q2020, Q2021 are holes carrying that take's questions, so (2021, 2020) and (2021, 2021) are holes; (2021, 2022)
# reads R of supply 2021, a hole after (2021, 2021): a hole.  Takes on a known 0 side are 0 whatever the other side:
# (2020, 2022) isn't an arc, 0.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index payers = [ewa, jan]
index yrs = year 2020..2023
input credit[sx in payers, o in yrs]: money PLN
input room[dx in payers, t in yrs]: money PLN
input carry_years: int

fill absorb
  supply credit[sx, o] for sx in payers, o in yrs
  demand room[dx, t] for dx in payers, t in yrs
  arc sx == dx and t >= o - 1 and t - o <= carry_years
  order o, t ties by pos(sx)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2020..
  known 2020-01-01
  credit[ewa, 2020] = ?"credit 2020?"
  credit[ewa, 2021] = 50.00 PLN
  credit[ewa, 2022] = 0.00 PLN
  credit[ewa, 2023] = 0.00 PLN
  credit[jan, *] = 0.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2020] = 30.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2021] = 80.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2022] = 80.00 PLN
  room[ewa, 2023] = 0.00 PLN
  room[jan, *] = 10.00 PLN
  carry_years = 1

ask f1: absorb.taken[ewa, 2020, ewa, t] for t in yrs law 2026-06-30
ask f2: absorb.taken[ewa, 2021, ewa, t] for t in yrs law 2026-06-30
=== expect
f1 (t = 2020): ?"credit 2020?" (credit[ewa, 2020])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f1 (t = 2021): ?"credit 2020?" (credit[ewa, 2020])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f1 (t = 2022): 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f1 (t = 2023): 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f2 (t = 2020): ?"credit 2020?" (credit[ewa, 2020])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f2 (t = 2021): ?"credit 2020?" (credit[ewa, 2020])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f2 (t = 2022): ?"credit 2020?" (credit[ewa, 2020])
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
f2 (t = 2023): 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
